[:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/4548"} "24 from 6 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The finals saw four nations competing, all with rich swimming traditions, and all with a chance to win the relay gold medal.  After one leg, Hungary’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/48222"} "József Munk"] " led by four yards in 2:40.8.  " [:a {:href "/athletes/45155"} "Frank Beaurepaire"] " (AUS) was 2nd, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/47246"} "Rob Derbyshire"] " 3rd (GBR) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/51394"} "Harry Hebner"] " (USA) in last.  " [:a {:href "/athletes/48260"} "Imre Zachár"] " swam the second leg for Hungary and increased the lead, reaching 400 metres in 5:27.2, eight yards ahead of " [:a {:href "/athletes/53949"} "Paul Radmilovic"] " of Britain."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The third leg saw Hungary maintain its lead, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/48213"} "Béla Las-Torres"] " finishing 600 metres in 8:10.0, leading by six yards.  But now in second was the United States, as " [:a {:href "/athletes/51308"} "Charlie Daniels"] " swam a great leg to pass Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/47264"} "Willie Foster"] ".  They finished their legs, respectively, in 8:15.2 and 8:18.6.  The race appeared to be over, with Hungary’s redoubtable " [:a {:href "/athletes/48187"} "Zoltán Halmay"] " swimming their anchor leg.  Mainly a sprinter, he went out far too fast, leading " [:a {:href "/athletes/51530"} "Leslie Rich"] " (USA) by 15 yards after 700 metres, with Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/47414"} "Henry Taylor"] " another five yards back.  Taylor caught Rich with 50 metres left and pulled away from him.  Halmay was now a shambles and swam into the wall only 20 metres from the finish, also allowing Taylor to pass him and win by three yards."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} 